    <mxCell id="dSH" parent="1" style="shape=folder;fontStyle=0;spacingTop=12;tabWidth=106;tabHeight=16;tabPosition=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#d6b656;" value="&lt;b&gt;horus.domain.shared&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;&#171;shared kernel&#187;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:10px;&quot;&gt;Provenance, EntityType, Gender&lt;br/&gt;DecisionBand (incl. ERROR)&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;CanonicalSlot&lt;/b&gt;  — moved here so&lt;br/&gt;ingestion and matching share the&lt;br/&gt;vocabulary without importing each other&lt;br/&gt;ids, value objects&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
      <mxGeometry height="175" width="425" x="1075" y="1035" as="geometry" />
    </mxCell>
    <mxCell id="tPROF" parent="1" style="shape=folder;fontStyle=0;spacingTop=12;tabWidth=114;tabHeight=16;tabPosition=left;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#999999;" value="&lt;b&gt;horus.tools.profiling&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:10px;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;&#171;tooling&#187;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot; style=&quot;border-style:solid;&quot;/&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:10px;&quot;&gt;WorldCheckProfiler, NarrativeProfiler&lt;br/&gt;NarrativeExtractorMain, SelfTest&lt;br/&gt;dev-time only — never deployed&lt;/span&gt;" vertex="1">
      <mxGeometry height="105" width="300" x="40" y="1260" as="geometry" />
    </mxCell>
    <mxCell id="nRULE" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#999999;dashed=1;verticalAlign=top;align=left;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin:4px 0 0;text-align:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;THE DEPENDENCY RULE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot;/&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:2px 4px;&quot;&gt;Every arrow points &lt;b&gt;down&lt;/b&gt; the page — inward. None points up. That is the whole test: a reviewer can verify the architecture by checking arrow directions.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:4px 4px 0;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Absences that matter:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 4px;&quot;&gt;• &lt;i&gt;matching&lt;/i&gt; has no arrow to any port or adapter — I-9 holds structurally.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 4px;&quot;&gt;• &lt;i&gt;domain&lt;/i&gt; points only at &lt;i&gt;domain.shared&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 4px;&quot;&gt;• no plugin imports another plugin.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 4px;&quot;&gt;• only &lt;i&gt;bootstrap&lt;/i&gt; sees adapters.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:4px 4px 0;&quot;&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;color:#b85450;&quot;&gt;Bold red&lt;/b&gt; = the two imports of &lt;i&gt;normalisation&lt;/i&gt;. One artefact, two consumers: I-10 enforced by the build, not by discipline.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
      <mxGeometry height="205" width="560" x="360" y="1255" as="geometry" />
    </mxCell>
    <mxCell id="nSEC" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#999999;dashed=1;verticalAlign=top;align=left;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin:4px 0 0;text-align:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;SECURITY BY DESIGN — WHERE IT LIVES&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot;/&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:2px 4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Segregation of duties&lt;/b&gt; (NFR-25): &lt;i&gt;bootstrap&lt;/i&gt; builds three DataSources and hands each repository only its own. The audit repository cannot UPDATE or DELETE because its credential can’t.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:2px 4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Secrets&lt;/b&gt;: read only in &lt;i&gt;bootstrap&lt;/i&gt;. No other package touches a credential.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:2px 4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Input bounds&lt;/b&gt;: &lt;i&gt;QueryName&lt;/i&gt; is a domain value object that rejects over-length input in its constructor, so every path — CLI today, REST later — is bounded.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:2px 4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Audit&lt;/b&gt;: an application use case, inside the ring. An HTTP filter can be bypassed; an interactor step cannot.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:2px 4px;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;No PII in logs&lt;/b&gt; (I-11): logging only in adapters; inner rings raise events carrying ids, never names.&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
      <mxGeometry height="205" width="560" x="940" y="1255" as="geometry" />
    </mxCell>
    <mxCell id="nLEG" parent="1" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#999999;dashed=1;verticalAlign=top;align=left;" value="&lt;p style=&quot;margin:4px 0 0;text-align:center;&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;LEGEND&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr size=&quot;1&quot;/&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 4px;&quot;&gt;- - - &gt;&#160; &#171;import&#187; / uses&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 4px;&quot;&gt;- - - &#9655;&#160; implements (port / SPI)&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 4px;&quot;&gt;grey dashed = descoped&lt;/p&gt;" vertex="1">
      <mxGeometry height="80" width="300" x="40" y="1380" as="geometry" />
    </mxCell>
